(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Writing Mathematics in Notebooks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"0efbd15a-ce49-46c4-ab73-4a3c319e0553"],

Cell["MathNotebook Tutorial", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"3d42636f-f813-4796-8cd4-5537b77c2779"],

Cell["\<\
How to write a mathematics paper in a Wolfram notebook: journal stylesheets, \
live referencing, and conversion between LaTeX source and native typeset \
math. Whether the mathematics is written as LaTeX or as built-in typeset math \
is your choice throughout \[LongDash] the palette only moves a selection from \
one to the other.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"63e4bb0d-4894-41d6-8994-0f4fa2583a30"],

Cell["Getting Started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0b9c3060-3487-41d2-be66-fb2fffd4afb8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After installing the paclet, restart the front end so that ",
 StyleBox["Palettes \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the stylesheet menu appear."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c7e9b12d-61e8-4ae9-a553-1f84a0297913"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Give a notebook a journal style with ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", or the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Apply stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu; ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in that menu takes it back."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"24e89e50-9ff7-4e7b-9ea2-f77953ef0985"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Style the opening cells ",
 StyleBox["Title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then write in ",
 StyleBox["Section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4a8b0fbe-d12f-4411-b9ed-90f1df4f0023"],

Cell["\<\
Every palette button acts on the notebook you were last editing, and on its \
current selection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"117ef901-757a-494e-ba8a-2e36f4a64f72"],

Cell["\<\
The journal stylesheets are light-only; applying one from the palette also \
sets the notebook to light mode, so printed and exported output matches the \
screen.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"feb74810-a014-4029-a334-61453f82835a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Update from cloud",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Setup",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, asks the Wolfram Cloud which version is published and installs it \
only when it is newer than the one you have \[LongDash] so checking costs a \
line of text, not a download. It then rebuilds the front end menus and \
reopens the palette, which makes the new palette, stylesheets and tutorial \
live immediately."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"50e1becd-ce7b-4e7e-a8a4-5a3c48258ea3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It always says which of three things happened: updated, with the old and \
new version numbers; already current; or the cloud could not be reached. \
Kernel code from the new version loads after ",
 StyleBox["Evaluation \[RightArrow] Quit Kernel",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the button will not quit the kernel out from under your \
session."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"68b00f7c-4e5d-4aac-8b67-789754da4b7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A copy loaded from a development directory shadows anything installed from \
the cloud, so the button reports that and downloads nothing. The same check \
from code: ",
 StyleBox["UpdateMathNotebook[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fe48b5a8-fe1e-4165-8a18-93ecfe2eed0b"],

Cell["Referencing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d6fb9477-593a-41a5-9122-c229d05c909a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select a numbered cell \[LongDash] an equation, a theorem, a section, a \
numbered item \[LongDash] and press ",
 StyleBox["Copy reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then paste into your text."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"133d0100-6d75-45e6-afd9-dca30fc7f5b1"],

Cell["\<\
The pasted reference is a live button showing the current number, so \
reordering cells renumbers every reference to them.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e095808a-01a6-4469-82d3-55e8bad00f0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clicking a reference jumps to its target; ",
 StyleBox["\[UpArrow] Go back",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns to where you clicked from."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cbf0a702-8a17-4bce-8a98-bdfbf4d405a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tag cell",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " names a cell, and ",
 StyleBox["Insert citation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " inserts a red bracketed link to that name \[LongDash] the two together \
give a bibliography: style each entry ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", tag it, cite it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a3211bd4-7cb1-4371-be69-f89f7fd7995f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tagging a ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell also labels it: the entry shows its tag in brackets in the margin, \
which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so the bibliography and the \
body agree without your typing either."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6f1ee178-ca33-415a-bd0e-771b023889bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a bibliography tagged before that was true \[LongDash] or tagged \
through the Cell Tags dialog rather than the palette \[LongDash] ",
 StyleBox["LabelReferences[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " labels every entry of a notebook at once, and clears the label of an entry \
whose tag you removed."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6891f3ac-7f88-4942-ba63-8cb5c85d29bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Existing tags are listed under ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Cell Tags",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"09febb10-21a8-41f9-a343-0bd7345ab95f"],

Cell["\<\
The theorem below and the equation after it are practice targets: select \
either one and copy a reference to it.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3d3bff04-6f57-44ec-b190-a71c55534128"],

Cell["The exponential map is surjective onto the unit circle.", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"dcd8a728-177f-4b36-8903-42172a6cc67f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", "\[Pi]"}]], "+", "1", "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"d4ab52ae-ead7-\
4e04-bc4e-cda505155ac4"],

Cell["Stylesheets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e0376a40-ab83-4e6d-a6f3-7c4d6d66e283"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four templates: ",
 StyleBox["AMSArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (amsart, Palatino), ",
 StyleBox["ArXivArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (article, Latin Modern), ",
 StyleBox["SpringerJournal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["RevTeXAPS",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Times)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"66629d97-232f-4cac-8c84-b7211eac865e"],

Cell["\<\
All four define the same style names, so switching between them is instant \
and changes nothing but the typography.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1091b6c7-5f0d-4dab-8feb-36452e7147c1"],

Cell["\<\
Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, Conjecture, Claim, Definition, \
Example, Construction, Remark, Question, and Observation share a single \
counter that resets at each section, exactly as in LaTeX; numbered equations \
count continuously through the document.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"feb7e449-e73f-458b-940e-ab1d111b85a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert environments from the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Insert environment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu, or with the ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Equation (n)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"af1ec082-b7a4-4f5a-8847-4e7147c1baaa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern and TeX Gyre are LaTeX fonts, not system fonts: press ",
 StyleBox["Install LaTeX fonts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " once to copy them out of a local TeX distribution (",
 ButtonBox["tug.org/texlive",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 ") into your user font directory, then restart the front end. They are \
installed for the whole machine, not inside Mathematica, so any application \
can use them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"583b77ca-c443-498b-9d28-416a8e297d05"],

Cell["Reading and Writing Comfortably", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"43eb7a04-e270-4cdb-b5fd-893a56490954"],

Cell["\<\
Each palette group folds: click its opener or its name to collapse it, so \
only the buttons you are using take up room. The palette remembers which \
groups are open across front end restarts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9d9e58bb-a86d-4bb0-a62d-25063129b67f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group holds two sliders and a reset. Like every other palette control they \
act on the notebook you were last editing, so leave the palette open beside \
your paper and drag while you read it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8ac10467-ed87-4bb0-b7cd-d97bb0fe5e8a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sets the size of ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and scales the title, the headings, and the abstract with it, so the \
document keeps its proportions instead of one style growing alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2c8a9843-977e-4251-8247-1114402d87be"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " does the same for displayed equations and their numbers, independently of \
the prose \[LongDash] the usual reason to reach for it is an equation left \
too small to read beside text you have just enlarged."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b51a6fb9-72e7-49e2-a000-35b85faf606e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both set real font sizes, so they reach the exported PDF. ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Magnification",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a different thing entirely \[LongDash] it zooms the screen and never \
changes print."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bff2b0f0-fbbc-4935-90fd-b2de377db52b"],

Cell["\<\
The settings are stored in the notebook itself, so they survive saving and \
reopening and travel with the file to a coauthor.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e4e81e61-39ea-45f3-9198-8c97eb5a87b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reset view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns the notebook to its stylesheet defaults and leaves no trace of the \
overrides; applying a stylesheet clears them too, since the new sheet \
replaces them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d03c402d-991c-40d3-975b-e58383b3896f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX cells are images and cannot inherit a style, so ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " re-renders each of them through LaTeX at the new size, from the TeX the \
cell stores."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"50a643b5-85a7-4dcc-8358-79102e92ce9f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["SetDocumentFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["SetMathFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] each takes ",
 StyleBox["Automatic",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop its own override \[LongDash] and ",
 StyleBox["ResetDocumentView[nb]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop all of them. They work on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " too."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bbc2dca8-0afb-4817-b095-b8538d2c0116"],

Cell["Math Input Shortcuts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"970bbb06-0356-421b-a0de-8098a25367be"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " inline math in text, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exits."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"20d580c3-70f2-4906-8f71-18cf37146dd8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+/",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fraction, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " square root."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9f4dac2b-fadb-441b-9937-56e89637bf2c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+^",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " superscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+_",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " subscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " switches between them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0edb6cca-87c4-4f23-a3e4-aa9250c3a5a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["name",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " enters symbols: ",
 StyleBox["a",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Alpha], ",
 StyleBox["el",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Element], ",
 StyleBox["->",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Rule]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"15408cb5-4c83-495c-9568-7393ca74cbae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " shows the cell expression (",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on Windows)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cc15d843-5e70-4e00-ac69-08ac822a0286"],

Cell["Working with Cells", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"55b63824-23a5-4834-9e96-6bd2b7d931d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Click a cell bracket to select the cell; drag across brackets to select \
several; ",
 StyleBox["Delete",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " removes them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a38476af-8d0c-4ef2-9279-0a22f3685130"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " extends the selection outward; repeat to reach the whole cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d92606c8-6a97-4f97-81da-6cc09fe012f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " restyle a cell: Title, Section, Subsection, Text, Input."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"73a78445-ce81-4017-9fd8-c0888fe4a774"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+D",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " divides a cell at the cursor; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " merges selected cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f4f5ee76-483a-495e-a52d-3eede6e54b2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " groups selected cells; ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ungroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2d095a8a-c6e8-4395-8216-b051253c44d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Double-click a group bracket to close or open the group; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+{",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " open and close all subgroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"79bb1487-43db-466b-b050-98a10627541e"],

Cell["\<\
Double-click a closed group's remaining bracket to reopen it; use Cell \
\[RightArrow] Delete All Output before sharing a notebook.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a6a8db8d-0958-4d4d-86d8-7b6f46c25078"],

Cell["LaTeX Conversion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ceb7084f-ea4d-48f0-89fe-8604f0ae3029"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select the cells to convert, then press ",
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". With nothing selected the whole notebook is converted."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"65e5d3d6-777b-4322-8da7-d4a61fb8fe33"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " parses inline ",
 StyleBox["$\[Ellipsis]$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\(\[Ellipsis]\\)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and displayed ",
 StyleBox["$$\[Ellipsis]$$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\[\[Ellipsis]\\]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; the starred forms stay unnumbered, the unstarred ones become numbered \
equations."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0ce8ae70-5d82-4461-b231-3a347a14dc51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " environment becomes a grid aligned on its ",
 StyleBox["&",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so it stays editable as one equation cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"67e2c199-9c85-46a9-9456-bdb3a4065595"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each converted cell keeps its original TeX, so ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back what you typed rather than a re-serialization of the boxes. \
Anything the parser cannot read is left untouched."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ede25c2e-00c6-4638-a506-6cfd283ce6e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input, Code, and Output cells are skipped, so ",
 StyleBox["$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in code is safe. To bring in a LaTeX paper, paste it as Text cells and \
convert."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ba81ccde-dc99-4fcd-9887-bad1a374c3f7"],

Cell["MaTeX", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2bed5791-4a28-4639-919d-b7d5a7e9e90f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX (",
 ButtonBox["github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"],
 ") is optional, and needs a TeX distribution and Ghostscript. It is used \
only by the MaTeX buttons; referencing, stylesheets, and LaTeX conversion do \
not."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8c2e5866-9c85-4623-870f-851c3b08992b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use it when an equation has to come out of real LaTeX \[LongDash] macros, \
",
 StyleBox["tikz-cd",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " diagrams, exact journal metrics."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"286fbaac-4ab3-4c71-8e92-d843cd47af36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Install MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " installs the paclet and points it at the local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fc84c70c-c002-4755-91ac-61fdb0003fa6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " renders the selected display equations through LaTeX; ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " restores editable typeset math from the TeX stored in each cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4c5fede8-07bf-49ff-a752-f10f057d59a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MaTeX preferences",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " opens your ",
 StyleBox["init.m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in the front end \[LongDash] deliberately not through the system handler \
for ",
 StyleBox[".m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " files. Set the preamble, the magnification, and ",
 StyleBox["$useMaTeXQ = True",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to route TeX typed into a notebook through LaTeX instead of the built-in \
parser."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"df0cfa89-50be-42da-bac7-84b832af45ae"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images: convert them back before editing, and keep rendering \
for last.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5d1940ee-dad3-43e0-ae83-9677b6cc934b"],

Cell["Best Practices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"832c7a0e-f909-4cf5-ad80-c74ffd5af5aa"],

Cell["\<\
One environment per cell, inserted from the palette, keeps the styles and \
counters consistent.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"59e77fbb-d353-430a-a95d-e97a5f8e18a7"],

Cell["\<\
Tag cells as you write them; tagging a theorem after fifty pages means \
finding it again.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"16080161-89db-4b6f-881b-560881687c66"],

Cell["\<\
Do not strip cell tagging rules: they hold the TeX source that makes the \
round trip lossless.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ec7fd68a-9885-43f7-89ae-3c39aa92e04e"],

Cell["\<\
Convert to LaTeX at submission time, not continuously \[LongDash] the \
notebook is the source.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"303dd829-dac4-4a0d-912a-4bd393d2aa16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before sharing: ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Delete All Output",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and convert MaTeX cells back to math so a coauthor can edit them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5de020b4-ba6c-4d38-b92b-fa2c304e4f9f"],

Cell["Credits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5573117b-90a9-44a5-a73f-23494be3a460"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The referencing scheme and the MaTeX integration are originally due to Nik \
Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"],
 "; this paclet packages and extends that work."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42e29aed-0ee8-4f1c-a9ea-59ce4a6a7992"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nik Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[murzin]"]],
 CellTags->"murzin",ExpressionUUID->"85dbcc49-7414-4aa8-927f-4320ddfd9ee5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Szabolcs Horvat, MaTeX: LaTeX labels in Mathematica, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
